dialogue trust_cleric_1
title: Steady hands
trigger: Trust cleric level=1
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker hero $with

node open commander
  The Cleric kneels by the wagon wheel with a bowl of fen-moss and a roll of bandage, mending the day's last cut. It is the Cleric's own, and the hands doing it will not keep still.
  * Your hands are shaking. -> shaking
    do: AddTrust $with 2
  * Nobody fell today. That was you, all of it. -> nobody
    do: AddTrust $with 5
  * I told you to sleep, that first night by the fire. You still don't. -> sleep
    if: FlagSet founding:watch_cleric
    do: AddTrust $with 4

node shaking hero
  They always do, after. Never during. During, they're the steadiest thing on the field. That was the first thing they taught me.
  -> taught

node nobody hero
  Nobody fell. Kind of you. But I count the ones who nearly did, and today there were three. That was the first thing they taught me, too: count.
  -> taught

node sleep hero
  I sleep. Just not much, and not deep. Healers learn to wake at a cough. That was the first thing they taught me.
  -> taught

node taught commander
  The bandage stops halfway round.
  -> white

node white hero
  They. The Choir, I mean. I wore the white once, Commander. Every collector rides out with a healer, did you know that? To keep the paid on their feet long enough to walk home.
  -> tables

node tables hero
  I stood at the tithe tables for six years. I held hands while they drew the colour out, and I sent people home I knew would never be the same. Then one spring I took my kit and walked into the fen, and didn't come back.
  -> ask

node ask commander
  The Cleric ties off the bandage and waits, eyes on the moss, not on the Commander.
  * You walked away. That's the part that counts. -> forgiven
    do: AddTrust $with 7
    do: SetFlag cleric:white_forgiven
  * Did you choose to go, or did something drive you out? -> asked
    do: AddTrust $with 6
    do: SetFlag cleric:white_asked
  * Then you know how the collectors work. I'll need every bit of that. -> used
    do: AddTrust $with -3
    do: SetFlag cleric:white_used

node forgiven hero
  Is it? Six years of tables, and one walk. I'd like to believe the sums come out that way. Some nights I nearly do.
  -> book

node asked hero
  Both. I chose, and something drove me. You'll be the first who asked which. Most people only want to know what the white looks like from inside.
  -> book

node used hero
  You'll have it. I suppose that's what it's worth now, to someone. I'd hoped it might be worth less.
  -> book

node book hero
  I keep a book, Commander. Names. I'll show it to you one day, when my hands are steadier than tonight.
  -> close

node close commander
  The Cleric packs the moss away, one jar at a time, and goes to check on the sleepers before lying down.
